! -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SHEATH SIGN TEST. Decides whether a_n's sign is wrong before any code is
! changed. See doc/sheath_sign_review.md section 9.
!
! Run:  jorek2_postproc < postproc_sheath_sign.in
! Then: util/analyse_sheath_sign.py boundary_quantities_*.dat
!
! THE TEST. At a strike point in ion saturation the conventional ion current and
! the ion parallel velocity point the same way along B, so with F0 > 0
!
!     sign(Jpar) == sign(Jpar_ionsat)
!
! Jpar is built from Jtor = -zj0/R (mod_expression.f90:1354-1356); Jpar_ionsat is
! rho*vpar*Btot = e*n*v_par (:1357). NEITHER goes through mod_sheath_bc, so this is
! independent of the coefficient under suspicion.
!
! PREDICTION: they are OPPOSITE today and agree after reverting a_n. If they
! ALREADY AGREE, the proposed fix is wrong - do not apply it.
!
! SECONDARY: Phi (:1757) contains no a_n. At a near-floating strike point it must
! read ~ +Lambda*Te[eV] volts, i.e. POSITIVE, order +30..60 V. It should read
! negative today.
!
! Both Jpar and Jpar_ionsat are BOUNDARY-ONLY expressions, hence
! boundary_quantities rather than pol_line.
! -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

namelist input

si-units
set nsub_bnd 2

! Early steps are fine, and preferable: neither Jpar nor Jpar_ionsat depends on the
! sheath BC or on convergence - Jpar comes from psi, Jpar_ionsat from rho and vpar - and
! the restart state already has the targets in ion saturation. A later step risks
! measuring a diverging solution instead. Adjust to steps you actually have (nout = 10).
! The analysis script handles several blocks and averages them.
for step 0 to 30 do

  ! R Z            - to exclude the X-point neighbourhood
  ! Bnorm B_abs    - to exclude grazing incidence (|Bnorm|/B_abs above sheath_min_bn)
  ! ne T_e T_i     - to exclude the density and temperature floors
  ! Jpar Jpar_ionsat - THE TEST
  ! Phi            - the secondary test
  expressions R Z Bnorm B_abs ne T_e T_i Jpar Jpar_ionsat Phi

  boundary_quantities

done
